WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.172 --> 00:00:03.805
miR-Network tests ceRNA hypotheses: does one miRNA bridge your gene–lncRNA pairs?

2
00:00:03.805 --> 00:00:16.239
Step 1: choose the species. For human, also choose the genome reference; we use hg38.

3
00:00:16.239 --> 00:00:29.014
Step 2: pick exactly one miRNA. Type part of its name to filter the catalog.

4
00:00:29.014 --> 00:00:36.894
Optional: add shifted or modified variants to compare with the wild type in the same job.

5
00:00:36.894 --> 00:00:47.854
Step 3: paste gene–lncRNA pairs, one per line. lncRNAs must be Ensembl transcript IDs (ENST…).

6
00:00:47.854 --> 00:00:55.863
Correlations are optional magnitudes from 0 to 1 (these are example values). An empty column counts as 1.

7
00:00:55.863 --> 00:01:02.045
'What will be submitted' shows exactly how each line was read.

8
00:01:02.045 --> 00:01:07.465
Step 4: the default settings suit almost every job.

9
00:01:07.465 --> 00:01:12.148
Step 5: review the job before starting it.

10
00:01:12.148 --> 00:01:19.343
Every tool available for the species runs, so ceRNA scores are comparable between jobs.

11
00:01:19.343 --> 00:01:28.549
The job runs in the background. Keep this page's link to come back to the result.
